<h2 id="aciub-contract" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Execution contract</h2>

- Loop: **`code → test → fix → test → …`**.
- Failures: fix properly and re-run relevant tests; do not ignore.
- Do **not** end an iteration by asking whether to continue.
- After green tests, continue to the next unchecked `[ ]` / next phase immediately.
- Never stop solely because a phase looks large (see **implref** §3.1c).

---

<h2 id="aciub-checklist" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Iteration protocol checklist</h2>

For each iteration:

1. Implement the **next** scoped chunk (prefer smallest green increment under the current phase). Runners/CLIs: **neat_logger** + checkpoint per **`.cursor/rules/neatlog-operator-logging-bar.mdc`** (INFO milestones; **DEBUG** when debugging).
2. Run **relevant** tests for that chunk (unit / Vitest / Playwright mocked e2e as the plan’s Quality bar requires).
3. On failure: fix and re-run until green or a true blocker.
4. When a **phase** (or major deliverable) reaches green tests: run the [**Exwar gate**](#aciub-exwar-gate) **before** marking that phase `[X]` or starting the next phase. Record outcome in the plan Decision log or phase notes when useful.
5. Update Tracker Documents ([§6–7](#aciub-progress-protocol)); mark plan `[X]` only **after** step 4 exwar outcome is recorded (append, or documented skip with cited story **N**).
6. Continue to the next iteration unless a [stop condition](#aciub-stop-conditions) applies.
7. Do not end with a handoff-only status; start the next chunk in the same turn when possible.
8. If backlog remains, do not send a completion-style final response.

---

<h2 id="aciub-exwar-gate" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Exwar gate (mandatory per phase)</h2>

**Exwar is a serious pipeline stage — same weight as “tests green.”** After each completed phase under **`aciub`**, execute **`.cursor/rules/exwar-war-stories-extraction.mdc`** (**exwar**) and **implref** §3.4 **before** the next phase.

A phase is **not complete** until this gate produces one of:

| Outcome | Required evidence |
|---------|-------------------|
| **Append** | New story **§N.1–N.5** in the correct file + that file’s **story index** updated in the **same edit** |
| **Skip (duplicate)** | Lesson **already completely covered** in **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES.md`** or **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`** — cite existing story **#N** and one phrase showing overlap |
| **Skip (trivial)** | Truly **non-significant** per exwar *What qualifies* (typo, chrome-only, no reusable mechanism) — one explicit skip sentence |

<h3 id="aciub-exwar-gate-procedure" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">5.1 Procedure (every completed phase)</h3>

1. **Read both collections** (story index + recent entries): **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES.md`** and **`war_stories/WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`** — dedupe against **written lessons**, not against product code.
2. **Extract candidate lesson** from the phase: trap, contract, design tradeoff, ops failure mode — prefer **mechanism** over “we shipped the checklist.”
3. **Default: append** if the lesson is **meaningful and not already completely covered** in either file.
4. **Route** per exwar §2.1: portable → **`WAR_STORIES.md`**; Floor35 / ops / IA / routes → **`WAR_STORIES_PROJECT_SPECIFIC.md`**.
5. **Write in-repo** when appending — absorb into **§N.4**; do not leave the canonical lesson only in the plan, chat, or `cursor_gen/`.
6. **Log in turn** (brief): `Exwar phase N: appended #119` or `Exwar phase N: skip duplicate #113` — so closing tables stay honest.

<h3 id="aciub-exwar-gate-forbidden" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">5.2 Forbidden skips (same class as implref §3.1c)</h3>

**Do not** treat exwar as optional homework or defer it to “later / user will ask.” **Invalid skip reasons:**

- “Mechanism already exists in code / demos / another scope”
- “Documented in the refactor plan or chat only”
- “Similar helper already shipped”
- “No time before next phase”
- “User did not say `exwar`” — **`aciub` includes exwar by default**

**Valid skip reasons only:** duplicate of existing story **#N** (same lesson text); or exwar *Usually skip* (trivial typo, pure polish with no trap).

<h3 id="aciub-exwar-gate-closing" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">5.3 Closing table (required row)</h3>

Every **aciub** stop ([§8](#aciub-stop-conditions)) must include a **War stories** row per **implref** step 4: list new **#N** entries (both files if applicable) **or** explicit skip lines with cited **#N** / trivial reason — never blank “none” without justification.

