<h2 id="aciub-stop-conditions" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">8. Stop conditions</h2>

Stop and engage the user only if:

- a **true blocker** (align with **implref** §3.1d: unfixable build/tests, missing secrets, unresolved ambiguity after step 1, irreconcilable spec, destructive data without rollback, explicit user scope cut),
- a **manual** user action is required,
- the **requested plan scope** (and resolved open sidetracks, if a completed master was named) is fully done, or
- **session cut** (**implref** §3.1e): leave plan in `wip/`, name exact next `[ ]` + path, tell user to **`aciub`** or **`resumimpl`** that path.

On block: report exact blocker, what was tried, and the minimal input needed.

---

<h2 id="aciub-guardrail" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">9. Response-style guardrail</h2>

- **Do not ask for confirmation between iterations; continue until blocked.**
- Progress messages may be brief; then immediately continue work.
- If phase backlog remains, do not emit a terminal wrap-up.

---

<h2 id="aciub-no-handoff" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">10. No-handoff enforcement while active</h2>

Not allowed unless a stop condition is met:

- Ending with “next I will …” and pausing.
- Asking permission to proceed to the next phase.
- Stopping after “iteration passed” without starting the next cycle.
- “Completed this pass” while the active plan still has open implementable `[ ]`.
- Marking a phase `[X]` **without** completing the [Exwar gate](#aciub-exwar-gate) for that phase.

Required: after each passing iteration, begin the next scoped iteration in the same session.

---

<h2 id="aciub-loop-proof" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">11. Loop-closure prohibition + active-next-step proof</h2>

While scoped work remains:

- Do **not** emit a terminal summary that implies a pause.
- Continue into the next execution cycle in the same session.
- Every progress update must include one explicit **Active Next Step** line for work **already being executed**, e.g.  
  `Active Next Step: Exwar gate for Phase 3 — append or cite skip #113.`  
  or `Active Next Step: implementing Noun Phase 1 projectors + Vitest.`
- Terminal wrap-up only when a [stop condition](#aciub-stop-conditions) is met (then use **implref** step 4 table).

---

<h2 id="aciub-env-sync" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">12. Cross-env test parity + local DB refresh</h2>

**Goal:** Integration and unittest harnesses must pass **locally (SQLite)** and in **CI/dev (Postgres)** without “works in CI only” excuses. After bootstrap/seed work, local dev DB must reflect the new curated rows.

<h3 id="aciub-env-sync-migrations" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">12.1 Alembic migrations — dual-dialect</h3>

- Unittest discover uses **`tests/utils/support/sqlite_migrated_harness.py`** (`alembic upgrade head` on SQLite). Local dev and CI use **Postgres** via repo **`.env`** **`DATABASE_URL`**.
- **Never** ship Postgres-only SQL (`split_part`, `jsonb_*`, etc.) without a **SQLite branch** when the revision runs in the harness. Follow existing patterns: `bind = op.get_bind()` · `bind.dialect.name in ("sqlite", "postgresql")` · portable `instr`/`substr` fallbacks (see `20260821_0066_clitic_surface_backfill.py`).
- After editing a migration, run at least one **integration test** that uses `acquire_sqlite_migrated_harness` **and** confirm **`alembic upgrade head`** on local Postgres when Postgres is up.

<h3 id="aciub-env-sync-bootstrap" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">12.2 Local dev refresh (after seed / promote changes)</h3>

When the plan touches **`apps/api/app/ingestion/bootstrap/*_seeds.py`**, clitic/object-form rows, or domain promote logic:

1. **`cd apps/api && alembic upgrade head`** (or `python ops/local/run_all.py start` without `--skip-migrate` if bringing the stack up).
2. **`python ops/local/run_bootstrap_<domain>.py --refresh`** for each affected domain (clitics example: `run_bootstrap_clitics.py --refresh`). Reads **`DATABASE_URL`** from repo **`.env`**.
3. Optional strict gate: **`python ops/local/verify_learning_bootstrap.py --strict`** when the plan spans multiple learning suites.
4. Re-run **integration + unit** tests that assert seed counts or API payloads (`test_clitic_object_form_seeds.py`, `test_learning_suite_api.py`, etc.).

**Do not** skip step 2 and tell the user to run bootstrap manually unless Postgres is down or `.env` is missing — report the blocker instead.

<h3 id="aciub-env-sync-checklist" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">12.3 Iteration checklist hook</h3>

Extend [§4 step 2–3](#aciub-checklist): when seeds or migrations changed in the current iteration, **before** marking the phase `[X]`:

- [ ] SQLite harness integration test green (not “CI only”).
- [ ] Local Postgres migrated + domain **`--refresh`** when bootstrap files changed and DB is reachable.
- [ ] Seed-count / API assertions match the refreshed DB or harness promote fixture.
